# promise: #722
# A click on the docked sidebar's empty space, under its rows, closes the open ⌘T bar, as Arc's does. Reported as
# leaving the bar open (GitHub #722, mdrubelamin2, 0.1.54, seen once in a recording). Not reproduced with a real
# click, through the window server (scripts/hid-click/click.m), on a page, in an empty window or after a space
# change; this pins that the click lands on the sidebar's own view and closes the bar.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
pace 0.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=sidebar-click
wait 2
cra://debug?mainFrame=100,100,1000,700
wait 1
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
# A real click on the page makes Cra the active app, as the reporter's was, so the bar's panel takes the keys.
click page-top
wait 1
cra://commandbar
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=before
expect-log Cra command bar rows before: open=1
click sidebar-empty
expect-log sidebar empty hit: SpaceListDocument
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=after
expect-log Cra command bar rows after: open=0
